<article class="guide-article bg-canvas py-12 md:py-16" aria-label="How to use a connection test without overinterpreting it">
  <div class="guide-reading mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 text-lg">
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">A speed-test result is most useful when you know how it was collected. Before comparing numbers or changing your internet plan, record the device, connection and task you were trying to understand.</p>
{% include "components/guide-start.njk" %}
<h2 class="mt-12 mb-5 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink md:text-3xl">Choose a test and a quiet moment</h2>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">If your internet provider has asked you to use a particular test, follow its instructions and keep that test's name with the result. Another public option is <a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="https://speed.cloudflare.com/">Cloudflare Speed Test</a>, which Cloudflare lists as a tool for measuring an internet connection. <a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/fundamentals/performance/test-speed/">See Cloudflare's explanation</a>.</p>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">A test transfers data and can affect other activities. Avoid running it during an important call or on a connection where you are concerned about data use. Read the test provider's information before using the external service; it is not a Naked Tech form. No claim is made that this is the application used on every service visit.</p>
<h2 class="mt-12 mb-5 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink md:text-3xl">Keep the comparison repeatable</h2>
<ol class="mb-6 list-decimal space-y-3 pl-6 text-muted">
<li>Record the device, room, time and whether it is using home Wi-Fi or Ethernet.</li>
<li>Open the chosen test's official page and follow its displayed controls. Let the test finish before copying its result.</li>
<li>Keep the names and units with the values. Note anything unusual about the conditions.</li>
<li>For another comparison, use the same device and test. Change one condition, such as the room, and record the change.</li>
<li>Close the test page when finished. You do not need to install a booster, change the router or sign up for a new plan to retain the results.</li>
</ol>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">nbn describes comparing near-router, other-room and practical wired results. <a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="https://www.nbnco.com.au/learn/optimisation/what-to-look-for-in-a-wifi-router">Read its guidance</a>. Skip wired testing if you are unsure about the equipment; do not move unfamiliar nbn cabling for this exercise.</p>
<h2 class="mt-12 mb-5 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink md:text-3xl">Read the labels, not just the largest number</h2>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Cloudflare distinguishes throughput, latency, jitter and packet loss in its connection measurements. <a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/radar/glossary/">Its connection-quality glossary</a> explains the measurement context.</p>
